    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 60 tests pass \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS, including the new `Cp14` (membership number uses fiscal year) and `Cp48` (returns `fiscalYear`) tests, with every existing test still green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July, named after the calendar year it ends in \u2014 e.g. a 2026-08-14 registration date is `FY27`).\n\n**`Owner.java`** (`model/Owner.java`):\n- Added `getFiscalYear()` returning `FY<YY>` derived from the (already business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`, backed by a private `fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` helper (`month >= July \u2192 year+1`, else `year`).\n- `getMembershipNumber()` now builds the `-M<YY>` segment from the fiscal year instead of the calendar year, keeping it consistent with `getFiscalYear()`.\n- `getMembershipPoints()` now awards the +3 tenure bonus based on **elapsed fiscal years** (`fiscalYearOf(now) - fiscalYearOf(reg) >= 1`) rather than a 365-day window. A brand-new owner still has zero elapsed fiscal years, preserving existing zero-tenure test expectations.\n- Removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**:\n- Added a read-only `fiscalYear` (`FY<YY>`) property to the owner response schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it; MapStruct maps it automatically from `getFiscalYear()`.\n- Updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nThe registration date itself (and its Saturday/Sunday/holiday business-day adjustment) is unchanged \u2014 the fiscal year is derived from that adjusted date, as specified.",
